      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A focused screening strategy identified thienopyrimidine 1 as a hCB2 cannabinoid receptor agonist with moderate selectivity over the hCB1 receptor. This initial hit suffered from poor in vitro metabolic stability and high in vivo clearance. Structure-activity relationships describe the optimization and modification to a less lipophilic purine core. Examples from this novel series were found to be highly potent and fully efficacious agonists of the human CB2 receptor with excellent selectivity against CB1. Compound 10 possesses good biopharmaceutical properties, is highly water soluble and demonstrates robust oral activity in rodent models of joint pain."
      },
